/**
 * A "location beacon" visual for the Contact page's left column, linking
 * out to MEP's real Google Maps listing (confirmed by the site owner —
 * not an embedded map, since a real Google Maps iframe would break the
 * dark theme and this project has no map library as a runtime dependency
 * for a static pin).
 *
 * The dot pattern below is real world-coastline data, not a hand-drawn
 * approximation: generated offline with the MIT-licensed "dotted-map"
 * package (https://github.com/NTag/dotted-map, land data from
 * https://github.com/johan/world.geo.json) at a small grid size, then
 * exported as one flat SVG path — the same technique the reference
 * design uses. dotted-map itself is NOT a project dependency; it was
 * only used once, offline, to produce this static path string. The
 * marker's position (72.39%, 50.94%) is that same library's real
 * projected coordinate for MEP's actual location (16.8406, 74.5909), so
 * it lands on India for a genuine reason, not by eyeballing it.
 */
